msgid "Migration Guide"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Today, we released Quarkus 2.14.0.Final with a lot of new features and small "
"improvements all over the place:"
msgstr ""

msgid "Upgrade to Jandex 3"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Include `quarkus-opentelemetry-exporter-otlp` into `quarkus-opentelemetry`"
msgstr ""

msgid "Additional Redis commands"
msgstr ""

msgid "RESTEasy Reactive: multipart form improvements"
msgstr ""

msgid "Support for caching annotations for Infinispan"
msgstr ""

msgid "Improved Kotlin support for Hibernate Reactive with Panache"
msgstr ""

msgid "Support embedding the H2 DB engine in native executables"
msgstr ""

msgid "Bump GraalVM minimum version to 22.2.0"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"As usual, the documentation also got some love during this release cycle."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"To migrate from 2.13, please refer to https://github.com/quarkusio/quarkus/"
"wiki/Migration-Guide-2.14[our migration guide]."
msgstr ""

msgid "What&#8217;s new?"
msgstr ""

msgid "Jandex 3"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Jandex, our class and annotation indexer, is at the core of Quarkus.\n"
"With Quarkus 2.14, Jandex has been upgraded to the brand new Jandex 3."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"The project has moved under the SmallRye umbrella and the `groupId` has been "
"changed to `io.smallrye`.\n"
"The package name was kept identical."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"It should be transparent for you, except if you have an explicit dependency "
"to Jandex.\n"
"In this case, while a relocation has been put in place, it is recommended to "
"adjust the `groupId` to `io.smallrye`."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Jandex 3 comes with a lot of improvements that will simplify the development "
"of Quarkus extensions."
msgstr ""

msgid "OpenTelemetry"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"`opentelemetry-exporter-otlp` is now the default exporter for OpenTelemetry "
"and has been included into the `quarkus-opentelemetry` extension."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"`opentelemetry-exporter-jaeger` has been moved to the Quarkiverse Hub: https:"
"//github.com/quarkiverse/quarkus-opentelemetry-exporter."
msgstr ""

msgid "Relocations have been put in place to simplify migrations."
msgstr ""

msgid "Redis"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"The work on implementing Redis commands in our Redis extension API continues."
"\n"
"In Quarkus 2.14, support for JSON commands, graph commands and probabilistic "
"data structures has been added."
msgstr ""

msgid "Infinispan"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Support for caching annotations has been added to the Infinispan Client "
"extension.\n"
"You can find more about it in the link:/guides/infinispan-client#infinispan-"
"annotations-api[dedicated section of the guide]."
msgstr ""

msgid "H2"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Until now, it was only possible to include the H2 client in native "
"executables.\n"
"Starting with Quarkus 2.14, you can also embed the H2 server in native "
"executables."
msgstr ""

msgid "GraalVM/Mandrel upgrade coming soon"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Quarkus 2.14.0.Final is still targeting GraalVM/Mandrel 22.2 but an upgrade "
"to 22.3 is planned for Quarkus 2.14.1.Final, which will be released next "
"week."
msgstr ""

msgid "In Quarkus 2.14, the minimum GraalVM/Mandrel version is now 22.2.0."
msgstr ""

msgid "Full changelog"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"You can get the full changelog of https://github.com/quarkusio/quarkus/"
"releases/tag/2.14.0.CR1[2.14.0.CR1] and https://github.com/quarkusio/quarkus/"
"releases/tag/2.14.0.Final[2.14.0.Final] on GitHub."
msgstr ""

